OL,3,GNEWSAAllotments become 'life-changing'
OL,4,Afor plot holders
OL,5,
OL,6,F"I could come up here and just be me.
OL,7,FIt became a place to grieve."
OL,9,FFor Kathy Griffiths, her allotment gave
OL,10,Fher a space to find peace following the
OL,11,Fdeath of her brother in 1981.
OL,13,FShe has now tended her own plot in
OL,14,FGroby for almost 40 years and said it
OL,15,Fhad offered her companionship as well
OL,16,Fas a space to grow food.
OL,18,F"My allotment means everything," the
OL,19,F77-year-old said. "I don't think you
OL,20,Fcould possibly put it into words."
